{
  "requirement": "TBV owns the model conversation, supported backend integrations, tool\ndispatch, and structured submission used by its ask builder.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject says TBV owns four things used by its ask builder: the model conversation, the supported backend integrations, tool dispatch, and structured submission. The reviewed tests cover each of them.\n\n**Supported backends.** `AgentConfig` in `config.rs` has three variants: Bedrock, OpenAI and Ollama.\n- OpenAI: `configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[supplied_openai_backend_runs_independent_calls_against_a_local_transport]` runs a real local HTTP server and checks four things:\n  - Each request goes to `/responses` with the configured model and `max_output_tokens`.\n  - Each request advertises the tools `read_node`, `outgoing_edges`, `get_next_page` and `submit_result`.\n  - The `submit_result` schema requires `result` and types it as boolean.\n  - The prompt contains the node reference and the \"Finish by calling submit_result\" instruction.\n  Its assertions also show that tool results are fed back on the second turn and that the saved evidence never contains the key or backend settings.\n- Ollama: `configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[supplied_ollama_backend_delivers_tools_and_results_over_native_chat]` does the same over `/api/chat`. It checks the bearer header, `stream=false`, the `num_predict` option, the `submit_result` schema, and delivery of the `read_node` result as a tool message on turn 2.\n- Bedrock: this backend is not tested end to end, because it needs the AWS SDK.\n  - `providers.rs#mod[tests]/fn[bedrock_native_option_types_are_checked_and_only_max_tokens_is_defaulted]` covers option typing and the `max_tokens` default.\n  - `providers.rs#mod[tests]/fn[cache_checkpoints_are_requested_for_caching_models]` covers cache checkpoints.\n  - `providers.rs#mod[tests]/fn[typed_client_calls_preserve_order_and_native_history]` covers normalizing client tool calls while keeping order and native history.\n  - Other Bedrock tests found in `providers.rs` and `configured.rs` cover SDK configuration and credentials. They are sufficient for the integration layer this requirement names.\n\n**Model conversation.** The tests below check that history and tool results are carried through each turn.\n- `tests.rs#fn[application_tools_preserve_graph_tools_in_the_same_conversation]` checks that tools persist across all turns. It also checks that results are delivered as `ToolResult` messages and that pagination state follows the conversation.\n- `tests.rs#fn[application_tool_factories_create_fresh_state_for_each_agent_call]` checks that tool state is fresh for each call and accumulates within one conversation.\n- `tests.rs#fn[behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer]` checks the system message and user message content that a request carries.\n- `tests.rs#fn[agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces]` and `tests.rs#fn[concurrent_tool_agents_isolate_histories_pages_and_submissions_and_share_reads]` check conversations and dependency traces under concurrency. Per-call isolation also has its own `tool_agent.isolation` requirement.\n\n**Tool dispatch.** The same tests dispatch `read_node`, `outgoing_edges`, `get_next_page`, `read_source`, `search_text` and application tools such as `increment`. They assert both the delivered results and the recorded dependencies. `tests.rs#fn[source_tools_keep_search_discovery_separate_from_delivered_source_reads]` covers the source tools.\n\n**Structured submission.** The tests above check the `submit_result` schema, including a typed review output in the behavioral-adequacy test. Scripted providers finish the conversation by calling `submit_result`, and the typed answer is returned. Finer submission rules (`submission.*`, `provider_failure`) belong to their own requirements and are not assessed here.\n\nI found no plausible violation of the subject's text that these tests would miss, and no unacknowledged gap.",
  "references": "152e27f9c9e7bc9c3e830b7fbfb7088f5da2327804c01b46add84e64cd3e0136",
